!scripts/alphaevolve/experiments/**/*.json
# P2-SR-RELEASE-01 — the GOVERNOR-signed production source authority.
# Tracked deliberately and by exact path: the runtime resolves it from the repo, so if it is
# only ever installed locally the harvest is not reproducible from a clean checkout. One path,
# no wildcard — a broader exception would silently pull in untracked local registry files.
# Its bytes are the signed representation; `*.json text eol=lf` above keeps them LF on checkout.
!source-registry/national-registry.json
# SOURCE-REGISTRY-RELEASE-HYGIENE-01 — superseded authorities, kept for provenance and replay.
# A quarantined object names the exact registry artifact it was acquired under, and that
# artifact may since have been superseded: the 144 objects harvested before the PUH size
# reissue resolve to reg-dv-puh-mmod-002, which is no longer in the active registry. Leaving
# these untracked would make historical verification depend on one machine's working copy and
# put them one `git clean` from gone.
# An explicit allowlist, not `legacy/**`: a recursive exception would make every future file
# dropped into that directory trackable by default, including unverified material. Each
# historical record is admitted by name after it has been classified. legacy/README.md needs no
# entry — it is not matched by the *.json rule above — and the inventories stay ignored pending
# a separate retention decision. drafts/ is now partially admitted below, by the same
# name-by-name discipline, where a committed test requires it.
!source-registry/legacy/puh-mmod-001-superseded.json
!source-registry/legacy/puh-mmod-002-superseded.json
!source-registry/legacy/geo-sources-superseded.json
# RC8 clean-checkout proof: the "pending a separate retention decision" above was overtaken by
# events. packages/mps-data-governance/tests/P2Auth03D1UnsignedLegalSources.test.ts,
# P2Auth03E3BSguWellGuidanceDraft.test.ts and P2Auth03E4BPlanbestammelserDraft.test.ts (5747b93)
# read these exact files by name; without them a clean checkout cannot run tests that were
# already committed. Same explicit-allowlist discipline as the legacy/ block above -- named by
# path, not drafts/**, and only the files those three tests actually require. The three
# puh-mmod-*-unsigned.json drafts remain ignored: no committed test reads them.
!source-registry/drafts/sfs-1998-808-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/sfs-1998-899-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/sfs-2010-900-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/sfs-2011-338-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/sfs-2013-251-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/sfs-2020-614-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/hvmfs-2016-17-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/sgu-groundwater-models-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/sgu-well-drilling-guidance-unsigned.json
!source-registry/drafts/boverket-planbestammelser-unsigned.json
# RC8-A — tests/unit/cesiumL0L1Fixture.test.ts (already committed) reads this frozen fixture
# scene by name. Same explicit-allowlist discipline: named by path, not public/cesium/**, so a
# clean checkout can reproduce the already-committed test.
!public/cesium/fixtures/l0-l1-scene.wgs84.json
!tests/fixtures/**/*.txt
!scripts/google-adk/requirements.txt
!prompt_optimizer/requirements.txt
!prompt_optimizer/requirements-dev.txt
